import json
from pathlib import Path
r=json.loads(Path('outputs/Binocular.app/Contents/Resources/research.json').read_text())
ctx=json.loads(Path('outputs/Binocular.app/Contents/Resources/initial-snapshot.json').read_text())['context']
lines=['# Binocular — Week 2 field notes','', '**Research reviewed September 15, 2026 · 2026 NFL season · @coffero**','', 'The best immediate improvements are roster-specific: add available quarterback cover in Jacked Pine, use a spare kicker slot for running-back depth in Netanyahu Ball, and avoid a panic tight-end trade in MSU Munches. These are research judgments, not guaranteed outcomes or submitted transactions.','',f"League ownership snapshot: {ctx['fetched_at']}. Player metadata cache: {ctx['players_as_of']}.",'',r['scope'],'', '## What the deeper check changed','', '- **Week selection:** Sleeper reported NFL week 2 while its display week was still 1. Binocular now defaults to NFL week 2 and labels the displayed score week.', '- **Availability:** the research checks full league rosters, not only the most-added players. Purdy was unrostered in Jacked Pine; Coker was unrostered in the two smaller leagues but owned in MSU Munches.', '- **Roster completeness:** Bowers is in reserve in Netanyahu Ball; a starter/bench-only view hid that context.', '- **Scoring:** completion points, passing-yard rates and yardage bonuses matter in addition to PPR and passing touchdowns.', '- **Meaning of the numbers:** adds are transaction counts, not distinct leagues; roster-count deficits are not a talent grade. [Sleeper documentation](https://docs.sleeper.com/).','']
for lid,lg in r['leagues'].items():
 lines.extend(['## '+lg['name'],'', '**'+lg['headline']+'**','',lg['strategy'],'', '**Scoring implication:** '+lg['scoring_note'],''])
 for call in lg['calls']:
  lines.extend(['### '+call['kind']+': '+call['title'],'',call['reason'],'','Assessment: '+call['confidence']+'. '+call['recheck'],'','Evidence: '+', '.join('['+r['sources'][k]['title']+']('+r['sources'][k]['url']+')' for k in call['sources'])+'.',''])
 lines.extend(['**Availability at the checked snapshot**','', '| Player | Roster status |','|---|---|'])
 c=next(x for x in ctx['leagues'] if x['id']==lid)
 for name in lg['watch']:
  p=next((p for p in c['market'] if p['name']==name),None)
  if p: lines.append('| '+(name+' D/ST' if p['position']=='DEF' else name)+' | '+(p['owner'] or 'Unrostered')+(' · '+p['injury'] if p['injury'] else '')+' |')
 lines.extend(['','Unrostered means absent from the checked rosters. Pending claims, waiver processing and subsequent moves can change access.',''])
lines.extend(['## Evidence that matters more than one box score',''])
for key in ['loveland','golden','douglas','black','coker_health','ladd']:
 s=r['sources'][key];lines.extend(['- '+s['finding']+' ['+s['title']+']('+s['url']+') ('+s['date']+').'])
lines.extend(['','## App and design research','', 'Binocular is designed as a personal football scouting desk: league selection on the left, a weekly game plan in the center, and a separate evidence view for decisions. The football identity uses field stripes, binocular symbols, numbered calls, an olive palette and cream scouting notes. Decoration stays behind the data so scores and actions remain readable.','', '| Research finding | Decision in Binocular |','|---|---|', '| League context is essential to useful advice | Show custom scoring and verify research candidates against every roster. |','| A user needs to understand why a move helps | Put the recommendation, reasoning, uncertainty and source links together. |','| Data and analysis age at different rates | Separate league-snapshot, player-cache and research dates. Explain that Refresh does not rewrite research. |','| Small Mac windows need flexible navigation | Add a collapsible sidebar and native View menu shortcuts. |','| Football decoration can compete with dense information | Use field lines in the scoreboard; use opaque, quieter cards for text and tables. |','| Small low-contrast text is difficult to read | Increase secondary text sizes and contrast; add zoom controls, keyboard tab navigation and textual status labels. |','', 'The navigation approach follows [Apple’s sidebar guidance](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sidebars). Legibility and keyboard work draw on [Apple’s accessibility guidance](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility). [FantasyPros My Playbook](https://www.fantasypros.com/nfl/myplaybook/intro) is a useful category reference for league-aware lineup, waiver and trade workflows; Binocular emphasizes inspectable reasons rather than a single unexplained score.','', '## What is implemented','', '- Binocular name, custom binocular app icon, football-field scoreboard and scouting-room styling.', '- Game plan and Scouting report views, with dated Week 2 calls for all three leagues.', '- Clickable sources that open in your browser, evidence notes and expandable conditions for revisiting each call.', '- Full-roster ownership checks for the curated research shortlist, with unrostered/rostered filters.', '- Reserve roster tab, detailed scoring, data timestamps and warnings when research and roster context diverge.', '- Current NFL week selection, corrected adds terminology, explicit limits on roster-count trade heuristics and support for commissioner-adjusted matchup scores.', '- Native refresh/view/zoom/sidebar shortcuts and saved snapshots that keep report text and metadata together.','', '## Next features worth building','', '1. **Custom-scoring projections:** obtain a permitted projection feed, apply every league’s scoring rules, then compare legal lineups. Do not substitute ordinal rankings for point forecasts.', '2. **Role trends across weeks:** show routes, target shares, carries and red-zone usage with dates and sample sizes, ideally through a reliable licensed feed.', '3. **Trade evaluation:** account for replacement players, lineup slots, manager needs and the value lost when a two-for-one trade forces a drop. Do not use an acceptance probability without evidence.', '4. **Persistent research refresh:** an explicit research workflow could update sources and archive prior calls. The current app refreshes Sleeper data only.', '5. **Broader Mac polish:** system light appearance, a fully native sidebar/toolbar, and a wider accessibility audit. The current app is a native Mac window with a local web-based interface.','', '## Limits and what to recheck','', 'Only one regular-season week is available for usage analysis. Published rankings disagree, injury statuses can change, and generic projections do not match every custom scoring setting. The current calls have not been backtested as a forecasting model. No waiver bids, trades, messages or lineup changes were submitted. Recheck final practice reports, inactive lists, ownership and waiver rules in Sleeper before acting.','', 'The research is a manually prepared edition for Week 2. It should be treated as archived after that week, even when refreshed roster data is newer.'])
Path('outputs/Binocular — Research and Design.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
